# Automat environments (maintainer LAN)

Authoritative hosts + prod rollout for the Automat Unraid stack. Full human runbook:
[docs/ops/AUTOMAT.md](../../docs/ops/AUTOMAT.md).

## Source of truth (version / health / admin UI)

| Role | URL | Notes |
|------|-----|--------|
| **Prod** | `http://10.10.1.202:8788` | Authoritative version, health, admin UI |
| **Prod theater** | `http://10.10.1.202:8791` | Lobby lightbox (LAN only) — not for QA |
| **smartmap** | `http://10.10.1.202:8790` | Household service. **Never stop** for Projectionist QA. |
| **QA sidecar** | `http://10.10.1.202:8792` | Ephemeral; Path B Hub pull only. **Never bind `:8790`.** |
| **Not truth** | `https://projectionist.automat.vip` (or ad-hoc SSH tunnels) | CDN/proxy lag; agents read stale versions here |

- Local `localhost:8788` is often an **SSH tunnel to prod** — not local dev; never use for e2e (see [e2e-port-8788.mdc](e2e-port-8788.mdc)).
- Appdata kit: `/mnt/user/appdata/projectionist` on Unraid; macOS SMB mirror `/Volumes/appdata/projectionist` is for **editing kit files only**.

## Agent prod rollout (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

When the user asks to promote Automat prod after Hub has `romwil/projectionist:X.Y.Z`, run **exactly** this — do not rediscover from shell history:

```bash
ssh automat 'cd /mnt/user/appdata/projectionist && ./rollout.sh X.Y.Z'
curl -s http://10.10.1.202:8788/api/health
```

`rollout.sh` is **Hub pull-only** (sync from `scripts/unraid-rollout.sh`). Never Path A host `docker build` for prod / CA proof.

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| SSH host alias **`automat`** | `root@10.10.1.202` (publickey denied) |
| Run `rollout.sh` **on the Unraid host** via that SSH | `./rollout.sh` from `/Volumes/appdata/…` on the Mac (no `docker.sock`) |
| Verify LAN `:8788/api/health` | Trust VIP CDN / random tunnels for version |
| QA on `:8792` Path B Hub pull when needed | Stop smartmap / bind anything to `:8790` |
| Prod promote **only when asked** | Stop prod `:8788` while iterating QA |

Hub-first ship order: [release.mdc](release.mdc) / [docs/RELEASE.md](../../docs/RELEASE.md). Docs-only PRs do **not** need Automat pull.

## UI verification

When the user reports UI missing/broken — **especially with a screenshot** — verify with **cursor-ide-browser** against the correct LAN host above. Do **not** argue from bundle string greps or “you didn’t scroll.” Trust scrolled-to-bottom + screenshot reports.

Interactive UI QA: [interactive-ui-qa skill](../skills/interactive-ui-qa/SKILL.md) → **QA `:8792`**, never prod `:8788`, never smartmap `:8790`. Adversarial UI proofs: [ui-testing-architecture.mdc](ui-testing-architecture.mdc).

## Ops UI (post-1.32.2)

Weekly newsletter + Year in Review: **Admin → Ops → Newsletters** (`/admin/newsletters`). Mail = SMTP/Resend/Apprise transport only. See runbook for Mail sticky-bar / iPad Safari footgun and YIR year defaults.

## Release lifecycle (pointer)

Follow [release.mdc](release.mdc). CA proof = Hub pull onto QA **`:8792`** (Path B), not Path A host build. After Hub publish, spin down QA unless a campaign is active. **Never** stop prod / `:8788`. **Never** stop smartmap / `:8790`.
